## Evidence in the tree this board actually builds

Verified against ChromiumOS's kernel, `chromiumos/third_party/kernel` at the
exact commit this board pins (`6a8a0d280f118a3f901ed2976255fef57b8261ba`,
branch `chromeos-6.1`) — not a vanilla kernel:

    4002  drivers/hid/hid-apple.c:389
            trans = apple_find_translation(swapped_fn_leftctrl_keys, code);

    4003  drivers/hid/hid-apple.c:999-1014 — all eight WELLSPRINGT2 entries
          carry APPLE_ISO_TILDE_QUIRK:
            J140K, J132, J680, J213   (APPLE_HAS_FN | APPLE_BACKLIGHT_CTL | APPLE_ISO_TILDE_QUIRK)
            J214K, J223, J230K, J152F (APPLE_HAS_FN | APPLE_ISO_TILDE_QUIRK)

Because the backport landed in 6.1.2, both changes are present across the
whole range of 6.1.y that openFyde R114 could build (6.1.25 here). They were
never needed for this board.

## Re-checking after a kernel bump

`verify-upstreamed.sh` re-runs these checks against any kernel tree:

    ./verify-upstreamed.sh /path/to/linux

It reports, per patch, whether the change is already present. If a future
kernel ever *drops* either change, the corresponding patch must be moved back
to `../files/` — that is the only reason to keep these files around.
